The spec: in_ready = !occupied || out_ready. The DUT has in_ready = ~full, missing the || out_ready. Also need consume/output behavior: when full and out_ready, accept simultaneously.

Let me write correct RTL:

```systemverilog
module ready_valid_slot(
  input clk, rst, in_valid,
  input [7:0] in_data,
  output in_ready,
  output out_valid,
  output [7:0] out_data,
  input out_ready
);
  reg full;
  reg [7:0] data;
  assign in_ready = ~full | out_ready;
  assign out_valid = full;
  assign out_data = data;
  wire accept = in_valid & in_ready;
  wire consume = out_valid & out_ready;
  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (rst) begin
      full <= 1'b0;
      data <= 8'h00;
    end else begin
      if (accept) begin
        data <= in_data;
        full <= 1'b1;
      end else if (consume) begin
        full <= 1'b0;
      end
    end
  end
endmodule
```

Wait — when full and out_ready and in_valid, accept and consume simultaneously, replaces byte, full stays 1. Correct.

When full, out_ready=1, in_valid=0 => consume, full<=0. Correct.

When not full, in_valid=1, accept => full<=1. Correct.

The interface order in original: clk,rst,in_valid,in_data,in_ready,out_valid,out_data,out_ready — matches. Good.

